158
00:12:41,676 --> 00:12:44,923
Read them yourself when you work the lab.

159
00:12:45,323 --> 00:12:49,600
First restore the manual standard and drag the shaft angle.

160
00:12:49,620 --> 00:12:54,990
Watch the loop bulge out beside the needle's scarf and the hook point pass

161
00:12:55,010 --> 00:12:55,791
through it.

162
00:12:55,811 --> 00:12:58,996
Note the readings, and sew 30 test stitches.

163
00:12:59,396 --> 00:13:04,773
Task one. Press scramble, which imitates a badly adjusted machine,

164
00:13:04,793 --> 00:13:08,616
and see which readings fall outside the manual.

165
00:13:09,016 --> 00:13:13,996
Bring them back in the order from the lecture. Timing first,

166
00:13:14,396 --> 00:13:21,302
then needle-bar height, and the clearance last. Then sew 30 test stitches.

167
00:13:21,322 --> 00:13:24,296
It's done when they're all good.

168
00:13:24,696 --> 00:13:30,930
Task two. Fit an Nm 110 needle, sew once without touching the clearance,

169
00:13:30,950 --> 00:13:37,356
and see what happens. Then bring the clearance back into the manual range.

170
00:13:37,756 --> 00:13:43,635
Task three. Switch to knit cloth, watch the catch window below get narrower,

171
00:13:43,655 --> 00:13:48,136
and put the working point in the middle of the dark green.

172
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:52,092
Task four. Retard the hook 10 degrees or more,

173
00:13:52,112 --> 00:13:57,534
and adjust only the needle-bar height until every test stitch is good.

174
00:13:57,554 --> 00:14:00,255
That one is also in the assignment.

175
