185
00:14:50,608 --> 00:14:54,937
Your assignment has four questions. One, calculation.

186
00:14:54,957 --> 00:14:57,316
With the approximate formula,

187
00:14:57,336 --> 00:15:03,798
find the shaft angle of catch for needle rises of 1.6, 2.0 and 2.5 millimetres,

188
00:15:03,818 --> 00:15:09,623
and how far the hook must turn on its shaft to go from 1.6 to 2.5. Two,

189
00:15:09,643 --> 00:15:14,792
the clearance was set at 0.06 millimetres with an Nm 90 needle.

190
00:15:14,812 --> 00:15:20,946
What does it become with Nm 70 and with Nm 110, what fault does each cause,

191
00:15:20,966 --> 00:15:22,915
and how do you reset it?

192
00:15:23,315 --> 00:15:27,531
Three, the lab. Retard the hook angle past 10 degrees,

193
00:15:27,551 --> 00:15:32,709
adjust only the needle-bar height until every test stitch is good,

194
00:15:32,729 --> 00:15:37,259
and use the slope of the window to explain why that works.

195
00:15:37,659 --> 00:15:43,639
And four, discussion. A T-shirt line skips badly. List at least three fixes,

196
00:15:43,659 --> 00:15:47,033
and say whether each one widens the window,

197
00:15:47,053 --> 00:15:52,559
moves the working point to the middle, or reduces the distance needed.

198
00:15:52,959 --> 00:16:00,299
Submit the assignment and the lab report on the WenQuest platform.

199
00:16:01,819 --> 00:16:05,266
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example,

200
00:16:05,286 --> 00:16:10,919
if the hook ran one to one with the shaft, would the loop cast off in time?

201
00:16:11,319 --> 00:16:15,489
If the timing is retarded and the needle-bar height is left alone,

202
00:16:15,509 --> 00:16:18,219
what problem does the window model predict?

203
00:16:18,619 --> 00:16:24,283
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

204
00:16:25,803 --> 00:16:27,466
Three things to remember.

205
00:16:27,866 --> 00:16:33,287
One: industrial machines use the full-rotary hook at two to one,

206
00:16:33,307 --> 00:16:38,473
spending an idle turn to buy time for tightening and feeding;

207
00:16:38,493 --> 00:16:42,213
the point moves at about 14 metres a second.

208
00:16:42,613 --> 00:16:48,405
Two: you can adjust three things, timing, needle-bar height and clearance,

209
00:16:48,425 --> 00:16:52,410
and a new needle size always means a new clearance.

210
00:16:52,810 --> 00:16:59,004
Three: the catch window slants and is narrow, narrower still for knits,

211
00:16:59,024 --> 00:17:05,830
so set timing, then height, then clearance, with the working point mid-window.

